# Apex -> www, preserving the full path + query (rarepond.com/rentals -> www.rarepond.com/rentals).
# www is the canonical host. This host-scoped rule only fires for requests that actually reach
# this Pages deployment on the apex hostname; it is inert for www and *.pages.dev. It exists so
# that the moment rarepond.com is pointed at this Pages project (added as a custom domain), apex
# deep-links 301 to www automatically - no separate Cloudflare redirect rule required.
# NOTE: today the apex is NOT served by Cloudflare Pages (its DNS points at an old AWS load
# balancer that 404s every deep path), so this line cannot take effect until that DNS is
# repointed - see the apex fix notes / dashboard steps in the deploy report.
https://rarepond.com/*    https://www.rarepond.com/:splat    301

# Rentals is its own static section - serve its files directly.
/rentals/*    /rentals/index.html    200
# Rare Pond Media is served from media/index.html at /media/ (Cloudflare serves the directory
# index just like rentals/index.html at /rentals/). Real asset files under /media/* keep serving
# static-first, so the page index and the asset library coexist. No custom rule needed here.
# Missing files under /media/* must 404 -- NOT fall through to the SPA below. Falling through
# returned a 200 HTML app-shell in place of the image, and the /media/* rule in _headers cached
# that wrong response for 7 days, poisoning any not-yet-uploaded /media URL. Real media files
# serve static-first and never reach this rule; only genuinely-missing ones 404.
/media/*    /404.html    404

# Studio SPA: any other unknown path renders the app (which reads the path and routes).
/*    /index.html    200
